%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dReally? I've been spending all my time at the office\nlately, so I didn't even notice.\d%K%P
「是这样吗？\n最近一直窝在这里干活，所以我也不太清楚」%K%P
The rain crashed against the window in fattened drops, its\nlow rumbling only ever interrupted by the occasional howl\nof the wind.%K%P
当当作响地敲打着窗户玻璃的大颗雨点。\n一边低吼着、偶尔发出横笛般高频声音的暴风。%K%P
Yeah, that did look like a typhoon.%K%P
的确，这是最高等级的台风。%K%P
%LCChief
%LC科长
\dThe bullet trains and airplanes bound west have all\nstopped. I imagine those that were planning to return to\nthe countryside for their holidays are now in a panic.\d%K%P
「西面的新干线和飞机似乎一律暂停了。\n盂兰盆节最后一天要到了，\n返乡特攻队要陷入恐慌了吧」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dThat sounds rough.\d%K%P
「那还真是糟糕啊…」%K%P
However, I was not thinking about stations or airports\nwith countless stranded people, but...%K%P
我虽然随声附和着，但浮上我的心头的，\n并不是遍布着迷惘人们的车站或者机场。%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dI wonder if they're okay...\d%K%P
「大家都…没事吧」%K%P
At the Terrace House Hinosaka, we had problems with leaky\nroofs and unstable walls even in response to average rain\nand wind.%K%P
就算只有一点风雨、\n都会漏进房子里的Terrace House阳之坂，\n实在是让人放心不下。%K%P
I seriously hope it will pull through this storm. It would\nbe pretty sad if I found out the house had no roof when I\ncame back.%K%P
到底，还能不能挺过今夜这场台风呢。\n在我回去的时候，房顶到底还会在那儿吗。%K%P
I was worried about them all, but...%K%P
虽然一直持续着这样的担心…%K%P
%LCChief
%LC科长
\dWell, I think we should start. There's no telling when\nthe local trains might stop.\d%K%P
「那，现在就开始吧。\n这边的电车也是，就算停运了也不奇怪吧」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dAh, yes.\d%K%P
「啊，好」%K%P
But now, I had to prioritize this battle.%K%P
但是现在，这场胜负才是最优先的。%K%P
Yasunaga stayed behind in the boarding house, so I was\nsure Mitoko would be all right. It was good we had so many\nshut-ins in these circumstances.%K%P
公寓的话，有八须永君在的话就没问题了吧。\n正是因为一直都在家里蹲，在这种时候才更值得信赖吧。%K%P
Things are gonna be fine... right? He wasn't going to\nsuddenly discover the passions of the youthful fruit, was\nhe?%K%P
…没问题的吧，他？\n不会突然发觉未成熟的魅力的吧？%K%P
I trusted him, but I was a little worried. Still, I had my\nown battle to fight here, and that required all my\nattention.%K%P
啊啊，虽然相信他，但还是有些担心。\n虽然担心…但现在重要的是这边的胜负。%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dI'm really sorry for making you come to work on a\nholiday.\d%K%P
「今天真是抱歉。\n本来应该是休假，还硬是让您出来了」%K%P
%LCChief
%LC科长
\dI don't mind. I live here in Tokyo, anyway, so it\nwouldn't feel right for someone who sacrificed his entire\nvacation to worry about me.\d%K%P
「没关系。我的老家本来就是在这里。\n而且被夏期休假全部泡汤的你担心，\n感觉总有些不好」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dThank you. Anyway, I'd like to start.\d%K%P
「不好意思…\n那么，还是开始吧」%K%P
I turned on the projector and began my P*w*r P*i*t\npresentation.%K%P
说着，我打开了备好的投影仪开关，\n屏幕上显示出P○WERP○INT制作的资料。%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dI will now explain my idea as to how we should review our\nrelationship with Mitsumaru Real Estate for the betterment\nof Michihama Trading.\d%K%P
「关于通过道浜商事的业务改善，\n重新审视和三丸房地产之间的关系，\n现在请让我说明」%K%P
I had only three days to investigate, gather evidence,\nplan, analyze, and predict the expenses and the effect of\nmy scheme.%K%P
这是我在仅仅三日之间，把包含调查、备份、计划、可行性验证、\n费用、效果测定在内的所有环节都拼凑出来的、\n极为潦草的资料。%K%P
But I couldn't complain about that. After all, we only had\na week left.%K%P
但是，除了匆忙完成外别无他法。\n再怎么说，这场胜负只剩下之后一周了。%K%P
Chief Director Shinayama and the managing directors that\nwere on the payroll of Mitsumaru were currently out on a\nbusiness trip overseas for seven days.%K%P
出差组的董事长和篠山部长，\n从今天开始，要陪同三丸总公司去进行海外视察。\n七天内不会待在公司。%K%P
We had to get as many supporters as we could during that\ntime.%K%P
在此期间，必须要尽可能多地增加理解者。%K%P
...%K%P
………%K%P
