%LCChief
%LC科长
\dKawakami's section? We joined the company around the same\nyear. We still share a drink from time to time.\d%K%P
「川上那边吗…那家伙和我是同一届呢。\n现在也经常和我一起去喝酒」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dDo you think he might join us?\d%K%P
「要把他拉拢过来吗？」%K%P
%LCChief
%LC科长
\dHe's already doing something really suspicious as far as\nthe company is concerned. We can make him, even if he\nresists.\d%K%P
「如今不安定的动向，\n拿这些威胁他的话立马就能成功吧」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\d...I would rather people joined us out of their own free\nwill.\d%K%P
「…可以的话还是请善意地让他参与」%K%P
%LCChief
%LC科长
\dI'm just kidding. He's gonna love this, I bet.\d%K%P
「开玩笑的。\n那个喜欢节日的家伙肯定一下子就会扑过来的吧」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dThat's very reassuring. It's gonna be all the more\neffective if this project comes from the real estate\ndepartment itself.\d%K%P
「这样的话就给我勇气了。\n这个提案，还是由房地产部提出效果比较好啊」%K%P
The managing director of our real estate division was Mr.\nTerakawa, who had transferred here a few years earlier\nfrom Mitsumaru.%K%P
房地产部的董事，是来自三丸调职组的寺川常务。%K%P
As such, Chief Kawakami, who was acting behind the back of\nhis boss, most likely shared our philosophy.%K%P
不通过那边就开展工作，\n那个川上科长，心里多半是明白一些什么的。%K%P
Actually, that made it possible that not even Chief\nDirector Washizaki was entirely on the managing director's\nside, as he should have been aware of what was going on.%K%P
不止如此，认可了那个行动的鹫崎部长，\n和他的上司寺川常务也有可能并不团结。%K%P
That seemed like the complete opposite of our Chief\nDirector Shinayama of the accounting department, who was\nan obvious lackey for Managing Director Miwa. I wondered\nif it was because he was closer to the fraud.%K%P
与紧紧粘着三轮专务的篠山部长掌管的会计部形成了对照。\n这也是因为比起打算盘的部门，那更接近现场的原因吧。%K%P
...Well, there was no point in thinking about that now.%K%P
…呃，这样就有些自虐了啊。%K%P
%LCChief
%LC科长
\dStill, I don't know what to say. It feels like we're\ninstigating a coup d'etat.\d%K%P
「但是该说什么呢…\n这样的话，简直像是发动政变啊」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dI never even dreamed I would ever be writing this kind of\nproposal.\d%K%P
「我也是做梦都不会想到自己会拿出这种提案书…」%K%P
All I wanted was a stable job -- peace and tranquility --\nbut yet again I ended up walking a tightrope above a\ndeathtrap.%K%P
明明这次我只想平安无事地在任期内规规矩矩地上班的，\n为什么总是会像这样陷入生死边缘的困境啊…%K%P
%LCChief
%LC科长
\dA mere chief and a newbie are trying to put two managing\ndirectors out of the company. That's unheard of -- almost\nlike a scene from a dream... or rather, a nightmare.\d%K%P
「科长和普通职员，还要排除专务和常务。\n怎么说呢，真是前所未闻，简直像是痴人说梦。\n而且还相当接近于噩梦…」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dAll we are doing is trying to get chief directors, and\nthrough them, other executives to agree with our idea, all\nthe way to the vice president. After that, all we need is\na sign from the president. It's business as usual.\d%K%P
「我们在做的，只是让部长成为伙伴，重役成为伙伴，\n副社长成为伙伴，让社长作出决定而已。\n和普通的结算并没有任何区别」%K%P
%LCChief
%LC科长
\dYou are... a terrifying man. I suppose that's to be\nexpected from someone who used to be a part of -that-\nKamata.\d%K%P
「你真是…可怕的男人啊。\n到底不愧是在那间镰田锤炼过的」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dYou exaggerate. I am just a laid-off employee; the bottom\nof the barrel.\d%K%P
「这说的…\n我不过只是个落伍的失业职员而已啊」%K%P
It seemed like Chief Hiragi had the wrong impression about\nme, since I happened to accidentally put on shoes far too\nbig for myself this time.%K%P
一开始，可能是因为穿着不合身的衣服吧，\n平木科长，似乎对我有着非常大的误解。%K%P
...%K%P
………%K%P
