\dEh? Ah, it's nothing. So where are you?\d%K%P
「诶？ 啊啊，没什么。\n那，你现在在哪呢？」%K%P
\dKansai Airport. All the flights to Narita were cancelled\ntoday. The weather over there was really nice, so I\ntotally wasn't expecting this.\d%K%P
「关西国际机场。今天没法在成田着陆。\n真受不了啊。那边天气很好所以大意了」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dOver there...? You mean Los Angeles? I don't think the\nweather there would have much to do with Japan.\d%K%P
「那边是…洛杉矶吗？\n话说我不觉得那边的天气能作为这边的参考啊」%K%P
\dOh, so you're making fun of me now? And here I was,\nbringing a nice roll cake for you from all the way over\nthere. Maybe I should just eat it all myself.\d%K%P
「啊～，也是这么回事啊。\n明明这次难得买了新式蛋糕卷的～。\n现在我一个人吃掉吧～」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dAh, sorry! I'm sorry! So what are your plans for today?\d%K%P
「啊～抱歉抱歉！\n那，你今天能回来吗？」%K%P
\dHmm, the bullet trains are not running either, so I guess\nI have no choice but to spend the night over here.\d%K%P
「嗯～，新干线也中断了。\n也只能在这里先住一晚上了」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dI... see...\d%K%P
「是、这样啊…」%K%P
\dAnd I was so looking forward to spending the evening\nchatting with you. Hahh... Luck has seriously not been on\nmy side lately.\d%K%P
「难得有好多和特产有关的话想和小都子分享的说～。\n啊～啊，真是倒霉啊～」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\d...\d%K%P
「………」%K%P
\d...? Toko?\d%K%P
「…？\n小都子？」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\d...\d%K%P
「………」%K%P
\dToko? Hello?\d%K%P
「小都子？\n怎么了？」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dEh? A-Ah! It's nothing! Yeah, well, it's a typhoon. No\nuse fighting nature, h-haha...\d%K%P
「诶？ 啊、啊啊，什么都没！\n这样啊，毕竟是台风，没有办法呢…」%K%P
\dIs everything all right over there?\d%K%P
「你那边，没问题吗？」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dY-Yeah, it's totally fine! The wind really isn't that\nbad! I think it's gonna pass by us anyway.\d%K%P
「唔，嗯嗯，没问题！\n风还没强到那个程度。\n台风好像偏离了这附近呢～」%K%P
\dThe news said it's gonna hit our town directly.\d%K%P
「但是新闻上说会直击啊…」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dW-Well, maybe it decided not to hit my house, then!\d%K%P
「这边也会有个体差异啦！」%K%P
\dIs that... how typhoons work...?\d%K%P
「台风…也有这么一说吗？」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dBesides, everyone's here with me. Mr. Retired, Mr.\nKumazaki, Yasunaga, a-and Ms. Kaya, and Mr. Laid-off...\neveryone's here...\d%K%P
「而且大家也都在呢！\n老爷子在，熊崎先生在，八须永君在…\n而且………夏夜小姐，就连失业先生…也都在呢」%K%P
\dI see, well, I guess if that man is with you, it should\nbe all right. ...As much as I dislike the idea.\d%K%P
「这样啊，嘛，那个男人在的话就没问题了吧。\n………虽说我个人而言，很是不情愿这么说」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dEh?\d%K%P
「诶？」%K%P
\dIt's nothing. Anyway, be careful. If something happens,\ndon't be afraid to ask adults for help, okay?\d%K%P
「什么也没有。但是也要小心呢。\n发生什么的话，一定要好好依赖大人哦？」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dI'm an adult myself!\d%K%P
「我已经是大人啦」%K%P
\dYup. I trust you, Toko.\d%K%P
「嗯，你很可靠哦，小都子」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\d...Thanks.\d%K%P
「………谢了」%K%P
\dAnyway, see you tomorrow. Sorry for making you wait\nanother day.\d%K%P
「那就回见了。\n比预定晚一天回去，抱歉了」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dThat's not something you should even be apologizing for!\nSee you...\d%K%P
「我完全不介意。\n回见了…」%K%P
...%K%P
………%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\d.........Seriously?\d%K%P
「………………………不是真的吧？」%K%P
...%K%P
………%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dAnyway, the first measure I proposed would only affect\nthe real estate department, and aside from promising\nsignificant results, it should be easy to implement while\ndoing little in the way of damage.\d%K%P
「就是这样，对策案１是这样的，\n对象范围仅仅是房地产部，而且效果也很大，\n不仅工作专心，而且障碍相对较小。基于这些判断的」%K%P
%LCChief
%LC科长
\dHmm...\d%K%P
「唔…」%K%P
And now for the third page of my materials. It was finally\ntime to introduce the proposal that could get ourselves\nout of Mitsumaru's hands.%K%P
材料还剩下三页。\n终于翻到了脱出三丸的提案这一页。%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dHowever, since the project requires increased cooperation\nfrom outside companies, we will require approval from the\nhigher-ups -- from a branch above even Managing Director\nTerakawa.\d%K%P
「但是，要是扩大和其他公司之间的业务规模的话，\n不管怎样都需要得到负责董事以上职务的结算。\n需要比寺川常务更有能力的人」%K%P
My first proposal was a rough revision of our real estate\ndepartment.%K%P
最初的方案，是房地产部的业务改善。%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dBut if we can pass that, the rest should pose no trouble\nat all. There would be little change in how we operate on\na daily basis, and most things will likely sort themselves\nout on their own in no time.\d%K%P
「但是越过这一关的话后面就不难了。\n业务内容也不会有较大的变动，\n对外的角度的话，也可以以温和的手段推进改良」%K%P
It was nothing huge, though. All I proposed was an\nincrease in deals with other real estate companies, so as\nto lessen the influence Mitsumaru's de-facto monopoly held\nover us.%K%P
虽然这么说，解决方法却是十分单纯。\n由于和三丸房地产以外公司的营业额被提升，\n与之相对三丸的影响力就被削弱了。%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dAs for the second measure, it deals with staff, and as\nsuch will require the approval of the Department of\nPersonnel Management at the very least.\d%K%P
「接下来的是对策案２…\n这就需要着手处理公司内人事的问题了。\n至少也需要了解手持人事权的经营阵容的情况」%K%P
%LCChief
%LC科长
\dYou want to re-assign some of the people, I see.\d%K%P
「要重新检查各部门的人员配置吗…」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dFor example, we have three divisions in the real estate\ndepartment with forty-five employees in total. But if you\nlook at our automobile department, you'll see we only have\none division with ten workers there.\d%K%P
「比如说现在，房地产部有３课、４５名在籍职员；\n目光转向销售额第二位的汽车部的话，\n１课、１０名也并不显多」%K%P
%LCChief
%LC科长
\dAnd if you look at the numbers, they are actually making\nmore money for us.\d%K%P
「光看盈利额的话，那边倒是赚得更多」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\d...Yes. A \dquality over quantity\d approach, if you will.\d%K%P
「…是啊。\n是个拥有着少而精的人员配置的部门」%K%P
Well, the real estate department was leaking its profits\nto Mitsumaru, so it wasn't so surprising they weren't\nmaking that much money.%K%P
不过，房地产部毕竟在向三丸提供着利益，\n利润少也是自然的。%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dIf you check other departments, they are all severely\nunderstaffed, with teams of ten or less; our real estate\ndepartment is obviously getting preferential treatment.\d%K%P
「而至于其它的各个营业部门，基本都是１０人左右，\n但明显都比房地产部要强上一截。\n…说明这完全不是人手不足的问题」%K%P
Proposal #2 dealt with escaping our dependency on real\nestate altogether.%K%P
对策案２，是让房地产本身脱去自己的依赖体质。%K%P
By increasing the business of our other departments that\nthus far functioned as an extra to real estate, we would\nfurther decrease the influence of Mitsumaru.%K%P
通过丰富一直以来被视作陪衬的其它产品的交易，\n减少房地产的成交量…\n进而削弱三丸的影响力。%K%P
%LCChief
%LC科长
\dOur company is well-known for its strong real estate\ndepartment. Wouldn't this hurt our image in the long run?\d%K%P
「我们公司到现在一直有着『房地产很强』的评价，\n这不会损害我们的形象吧？」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dI don't believe so. I made a graph depicting the\nindividual income and expenditure of all our departments.\d%K%P
「我觉得几乎不会。\n这边有房地产之外的收支状况的图表」%K%P
%LCChief
%LC科长
\dWhen you look at it like this, it seems like our company\nis doing a pretty steady job, all things concerned.\d%K%P
「这么一看…\n我们公司不是干得挺踏实的吗」%K%P
The chief smiled proudly upon looking at my graph.%K%P
看着准备好的补充材料中的图表，\n科长略带自豪地点着头。%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dTo tell the truth, I see little point in us staying in\nMitsumaru's shadow. Looking at these profits, our company\ncould have gone independent years ago.\d%K%P
「说实在的，感觉并没有藏在大树树荫底下的必要性。\n从数年前开始，就本应该进行非常独立的核算了」%K%P
%LCChief
%LC科长
\dI imagine these things were set in motion when our\ncompany was established. It's probably not as easy to\nachieve as it sounds.\d%K%P
「因为创立的背景横纵交错，\n也许是被各种阻碍束缚住了啊…」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\d...It's a good company. If possible, I'd like to ensure I\nhave a future here.\d%K%P
「…真是好公司啊。\n可以的话，真想把自己的骨灰埋在这里呢」%K%P
Putting aside the reason behind its establishment, the\nstaff they acquired over the years was too talented to be\nsimply let go.%K%P
与公司兴旺的原因无关，\n这里依然集中了非常优秀的人才，取得了实实在在的成果。%K%P
They did their best for many years despite their efforts\nbringing only minimal profits due to Mitsumaru's scheme.%K%P
不管如何努力每年仍然不知为何只能达成收支平衡，\n而面对这样的现状他们仍然没有失去干劲不断努力着。%K%P
It might not sound like much on paper, but being able to\npersevere in such conditions was a grand feat not many men\nwere capable of.%K%P
这种精神实在是宝贵啊。%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dNext, the third measure... You could say it's an improved\nand more drastic version of the second.\d%K%P
「接下来的是对策案３…\n比起案２来，这是更进一步的推进」%K%P
%LCChief
%LC科长
\dThe disbanding of the real estate department...\d%K%P
「房地产部解体…」%K%P
Measure #2 was about putting all departments on equal\nground, while measure #3 meant doing away with all that\nwas holding us back.%K%P
与试图将包含不动产部的各部平均化的案２相对，\n这是排除房地产部，实现各部的平均化。%K%P
In other words, it meant re-assigning all the forty-five\npeople in real estate to our other five sales departments.%K%P
单纯地说，\n就是将房地产部的４５人，全数分配到剩下的５个营业系部门之中。%K%P
That would mean an almost twofold increase in most of\nthem, which would, in turn, mean more business and more\nprofit... probably.%K%P
各部门的规模几乎翻倍，\n会焕发比起现在更大的活力吧…大概。%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dIf we go that far, we can eliminate the influence of\nMitsumaru completely. I mean, we wouldn't be dealing in\ntheir business at all.\d%K%P
「做到这一步的话，\n三丸房地产的影子就会被漂亮地完全消去。\n毕竟他们已经不可能再干涉房地产了」%K%P
%LCChief
%LC科长
\dI don't think they would just take that lying down.\d%K%P
「三丸大概不会保持沉默吧」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dBy that time, they will no longer be a business with\nenough power to do anything about it.\d%K%P
「到那时候，他们就不再是能发挥\n现有影响力的企业了」%K%P
%LCChief
%LC科长
\d...\d%K%P
「………」%K%P
I knew that comment would make the chief grimace.%K%P
听着我说的话，\n科长的脸果然紧紧地皱成了一团。%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dYou could say that my proposed measures are improvement,\nreformation, and finally revolution, in that order. I\nwould like to implement them slowly, but...\d%K%P
「从案１开始，依次是改善、改革、革命的感觉吧。\n如果可能的话，我倒是很想慢慢地逐步推进…」%K%P
%LCChief
%LC科长
\dWe don't have the time...\d%K%P
「但是，剩余的时间就…是吧」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dExactly. We need to show results as soon as possible.\d%K%P
「就是这样。\n想快点出成果的话顺序就要反过来」%K%P
It would all come crashing down this autumn. We had a time\nlimit.%K%P
胜负就在秋天。\n我们的时间最开始就被限制了。%K%P
As such, it wouldn't be enough to just start from mere\nimprovement. We needed quick reforms -- perhaps even a\nfull-blown revolution.%K%P
所以说现在，不应该推行本来应该推进的改善，\n而是只有推进改革、不、革命的进行。%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dFinally, I have a fourth measure prepared. To tell the\ntruth, I am still not sure if I should even mention it\nduring our main presentation.\d%K%P
「最后的是，对策案４…\n说实话，后面的具体事宜我还在犹豫到底要不要进行说明」%K%P
%LCChief
%LC科长
\dWhy?\d%K%P
「为什么呢？」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dIt is a fairly... drastic measure.\d%K%P
「这是一个刺激性很强的提案…」%K%P
All we needed was approval from the top. It was a move\nthat would completely turn the tables on that crucial day.%K%P
需要的只有最顶级的当机立断。\n迫近的期限根本不算什么，是一步直接逆转的棋。%K%P
But one could also call it a deal with the devil that in a\nsense flipped over the very heart and soul of this\ncompany.%K%P
但那是在某种意义上，从根基颠覆这个公司创立意义的、\n与恶魔之间的交易。%K%P
If they agreed to this, Michihama Trading would certainly\nsurvive, and likely end up much stronger than before.%K%P
借助这个提案，道浜商事大概是可以活下来的。\n而且有很大的可能取得比现在更好的业绩。%K%P
The only issue was that the surviving firm might not be\ncalled Michihama Trading anymore.%K%P
但是那个时候，活下来的道浜商事，\n究竟还是不是道浜商事原来的样子呢…%K%P
%LCChief
%LC科长
\dYoshimura...\d%K%P
「芳村君…」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dI don't think it's a good idea after all. Let's skip this\npage and move on to the summary.\d%K%P
「果然还是算了吧。\n跳过这一页，看一下最后的总结…」%K%P
%LCChief
%LC科长
\dYoshimura.\d%K%P
「芳村君」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dEh? Ah, yes?\d%K%P
「诶？啊，是？」%K%P
%LCChief
%LC科长
\dShow me what you have, and we can think about this\ntogether.\d%K%P
「让我看一下。\n在此基础上，我们两人试着考虑一下吧」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dEh...?\d%K%P
「诶…？」%K%P
%LCChief
%LC科长
\dI'm not going to force you to carry all the\nresponsibility alone.\d%K%P
「不能让你一个人承担责任啊」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dBut Chief, you have...\d%K%P
「不，但对科长来说…」%K%P
A wife, and a child soon to attend university...%K%P
夫人、还有快要考大学的儿子…%K%P
%LCChief
%LC科长
\dYou originally got me involved to have more influence for\nyour ideas, is that not the case? Surely there's no more\nneed for secrecy after coming this far.\d%K%P
「再说了，要达成各部门的调整的话，我就已经被卷进来了吧？\n你觉得我事到如今还藏得住吗？」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\d...Chief Hiragi.\d%K%P
「………平木科长」%K%P
%LCChief
%LC科长
\dWell then, continue. By the way, your explanations are a\ntouch too long and technical for a presentation. You\nshould try to write a script and practice speaking so the\nwhole thing doesn't take more than ten minutes.\d%K%P
「好了，继续吧。\n但这个方案的说明太花时间了。\n最好控制在１０分钟之内，调整一下阐述方式吧」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dAh, I'm sorry about that.\d%K%P
「抱、抱歉」%K%P
%LCChief
%LC科长
\dThe materials you prepared are very good, but you should\ntry to speak in a louder voice, and more clearly with no\ndigressions. Also, your voice occasionally gains that odd\nsqueaking quality.\d%K%P
「芳村君的资料非常好，但是陈述还存在着问题呢。\n声音要更大一些，说得更流畅、更简明扼要一些。\n…而且，经常用假声也是减分点呢」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dA...Aha... Ahaha...\d%K%P
「啊…啊哈、啊哈哈…」%K%P
Was I really so squeaky all the time...?%K%P
我的声音…有那么尖吗…？%K%P
%LCChief
%LC科长
\dWhat's wrong? Did you get tired? Well, I cannot blame\nyou. I imagine you didn't have much time to sleep. Need a\nbreather?\d%K%P
「怎么了？是有些累了吗？\n嘛，也不要勉强，你一直在通宵的吧。\n要休息一下吗？」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dNot really, but if possible, can I just get one minute?\d%K%P
「不，可是………抱歉，就一分钟」%K%P
In an attempt to avoid showing my face, I turned towards\nthe window -- it was still being relentlessly bombarded by\nlarge droplets of rain.%K%P
我不想让别人看到自己的脸，\n于是注视着仍然承受雨滴激烈敲打的窗户玻璃外面。%K%P
The wind, too, had grown in intensity; the trees below our\nwindow swayed violently in the storm.%K%P
风比起刚才吹得更大，\n窗户下面街道旁边的树，向旁边倾斜得更厉害了。%K%P
%LCChief
%LC科长
\dTo think a typhoon would be raging during such a drastic\nshift in this company's life... To be honest, I haven't\nfelt this excited in years.\d%K%P
「但是这算啥啊，公司的危机再加上这台风。\n我都这么一把年纪了，心还砰砰直跳」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dAhaha...\d%K%P
「啊哈哈…」%K%P
%LCChief
%LC科长
\dI'm not even talking about our own fate. The lives of all\nthe people who belong to this company rest in our hands\nnow.\d%K%P
「毕竟现在，别说是自己的人生，\n现在这个公司全体职员的人生都握在手上啊」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dI wish it didn't, to tell you the truth.\d%K%P
「虽然十分地不情愿…」%K%P
%LCChief
%LC科长
\dI feel the same. All I ever wanted was another fifteen\nyears of peace and quiet until retirement.\d%K%P
「就算我也是如此。\n离退休只剩１５年了。\n我本来是想希望平稳度过的」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dAh...\d%K%P
「啊…」%K%P
%LCChief
%LC科长
\dYou know, when the director of personnel introduced you\nto me, my first impression was that you were an aspirer of\ntranquility, just like me. I thought we would find\nourselves on the same page right away.\d%K%P
「说起来啊，人事科长向我介绍你时，我的第一印象是\n『啊啊，这家伙肯定和我一样信奉得过且过主义。\n如果真是如此，应该能和我好好相处的』」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\d...\d%K%P
「………」%K%P
%LCChief
%LC科长
\dBut then you go and -- for lack of a better word --\noutright attack our chief director on your first week...\nWell, that alone took two years off my life.\d%K%P
「结果怎么会想到…\n入社一周内就顶撞了部长。\n光那一会儿我的寿命就得缩短了两年呐」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\d...Chief.\d%K%P
「………科长」%K%P
%LCChief
%LC科长
\dYou're trying to apologize for it now? It's a bit too\nlate for that, if you ask me.\d%K%P
「事到如今再道歉已经晚了哦？\n毕竟已经被卷入到这个地步了」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dHave you ever participated in a disaster drill before?\d%K%P
「您接受过避难训练吗？」%K%P
%LCChief
%LC科长
\dWhat are you talking about?\d%K%P
「指的是？」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dI'm talking about when an announcement along the lines of\n\dearthquake is in progress, please seek cover under the\nnearest desk\d plays from the speakers. You know, on\ndisaster prevention day, for example.\d%K%P
「就是『当地震发生的时候，请到桌子底下避难』\n这种，一直在电视上播出的东西。在防灾日什么的」%K%P
%LCChief
%LC科长
\dWell, they make us do that about once a year. What of\nit?\d%K%P
「那个嘛…每年都会有这么一出呢。\n不过，说这个是？」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\d...I think an earthquake's about to happen in Kanto.\d%K%P
「…关东地区，发生了地震」%K%P
%LCChief
%LC科长
\dWhat are you talking about? It's a typhoon, not a--\d%K%P
「你在说什么呢？\n现在不是地震而是台风…」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\d...Please, just hide under your desk, quickly! And don't\nmake a sound!\d%K%P
「…请到桌子底下避难，快点！\n绝对不能出声！」%K%P
%LCChief
%LC科长
\dY-Yoshimura...?\d%K%P
「芳、芳村君…？」%K%P
Below our window, among the swaying trees...%K%P
窗外，被吹得摇摇晃晃的、歪向一边的行道树…%K%P
...in the very middle of the storm, I spotted Chief\nDirector Shinayama getting out of a parked taxi.%K%P
接下来，在暴风雨中，从出租车中冲出来、闯入楼中的，是篠山部长。%K%P
.........%K%P
………%K%P
......%K%P
……%K%P
...%K%P
…%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dHaha... Hahaha...\d%K%P
「哈哈…哈哈哈…」%K%P
Wednesday, August 15th, 10 PM.%K%P
８月１５日 星期三 晚上１０时。%K%P
I was on my way to the station, having just left Michihama\nTrading's main building.%K%P
离开道浜商事，走在去往车站的路上。%K%P
I was carrying a heavy bag...%K%P
两手拿着的包非常重…\n不，这个就完全没关系了。%K%P
...and made a raspy chuckle as the falling rain moistened\nmy face.%K%P
干涸的笑声，和雨滴一起奔淌着。%K%P
In the bag there was packed emergency medicine, washed\nlunch boxes, unopened souvenir bags, and a sweater that\nshe thought might be of use.%K%P
包里装着的，是一套常备药、\n洗好的便当盒、没有开封的特产，以及，\n也许现在可以派上用场的毛衣。%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\d...Khh.\d%K%P
「呼…唔…」%K%P
The rain soaked into both my suit and the bag, slowing my\nalready sluggish pace even further.%K%P
渗入西服和包里的雨，\n让本来就已经十分沉重的身体承受着越来越大的负荷，\n迈向前方的步履，也变得越发沉重。%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dThank you... very much...\d%K%P
「受你们…照顾了」%K%P
I looked back one final time to glance at a now-darkened\nwindow on Michihama Trading's main building.%K%P
接下来，我最后再一次地，\n向着现在已经关上了灯的道浜商事大楼的窗户回望。%K%P
%LCChief
%LC部长
\d\dYou've been caught red-handed.\d\d%K%P
『决定性的啊…』%K%P
%LCChief
%LC部长
\d\dToo bad for you, Yoshimura. You were so close to luring\nme into a trap.\d\d%K%P
『运气真差呢芳村君…\n明明只差一点，我可能就要掉到圈套中了』%K%P
%LCChief
%LC部长
\d\dWhat is the meaning of these documents? What was your\naim in joining our company?\d\d%K%P
『这到底是什么资料？\n你到底是带着什么目的，进入我们公司的？』%K%P
%LCChief
%LC部长
\d\dDo you still intend to play the fool? In that case,\nallow me to rephrase my question. Who is paying you to\ntear us apart?\d\d%K%P
『打算装傻吗？\n那，要让我单刀直入地问吗？\n你到底受雇于谁，才染指这种行为的？』%K%P
%LCChief
%LC部长
\d\dGiving me the silent treatment? I imagine that's exactly\nwhat you did at Kamata before they let you go.\d\d%K%P
『不说话吗？\n大概在镰田也是用了同样的手法，\n你才被公司开除的吧？』%K%P
%LCChief
%LC部长
\d\dWell, it hardly matters. After all, you will never be\nshowing your face in here again.\d\d%K%P
『算了，也罢。\n毕竟不管怎样，我都不想再看到你的脸了』%K%P
%LCChief
%LC部长
\d\dRemember this well, Yoshimura Osamu. Your name will be\nblacklisted throughout this entire business. I will\npersonally see to that.\d\d%K%P
『给我记好了…芳村理君。\n从明天开始，你的名字将会被深深刻在这个业界的黑名单上』%K%P
%LCChief
%LC部长
\d\dSo give up on believing you will ever find a proper job\never again.\d\d%K%P
『别想再次就职了』%K%P
I underestimated this typhoon...%K%P
太小看这场台风了…%K%P
Narita airport had to cancel all its flights, which ended\nup delaying the chief director's business trip.%K%P
成田机场全面停运，\n本来要去海外出差的部长也去不成了。%K%P
He thought to drop by the company on his way back home,\nand discovered us by mere \dcoincidence\d.%K%P
因此，就『偶然』地返回了一次公司。%K%P
The three days I spent without proper sleep must've made\nme unable to predict this otherwise completely obvious\nscenario.%K%P
通了三宵的头脑，疏忽了这么简单的预判，\n大概是疲惫过头了。%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dHahh...\d%K%P
「哈啊…」%K%P
I lost my job again.%K%P
再一次，失去了工作。%K%P
Not to mention, there was the added \dwonderful\d bonus of\nnever being able to find employment at a sales company for\nthe rest of my life.%K%P
不光如此，这一次的事态，\n让我被加上了『无法再次获得商事系工作』\n这种“迷人”的属性。%K%P
It seemed like I finally managed to completely burn all\nthe bridges with the only field of work I was trained for.%K%P
终于，连我唯一的『本业』，\n大门也就这样关闭了。%K%P
The more effort I put in, the worse everything went. Could\nit be that there really was something about me that made\nme unfit to properly function in society?%K%P
越是努力工作，事态越是恶化…\n难道我，真的不适合这个社会吗？%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dWell, I'm just glad he didn't find Chief Hiragi, at\nleast.\d%K%P
「不过啊，平木科长没被看到真是太好了」%K%P
That was the only silver lining I could see amidst today's\nmassive maelstrom of despair.%K%P
这是完全枯萎的我，在绝望之中最后的救赎。%K%P
I think I did a good job averting the chief director's\nattention from the desk my friend was hiding under.%K%P
藏起科长那个时候自己的机智，\n是值得受到赞美的吧。%K%P
Still...%K%P
不过啊…%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dWhat am I going to do now...?\d%K%P
「今后，该怎么办呢…」%K%P
The rain had gotten so intense, I felt as though I\ncouldn't take another step forward.%K%P
倾盆而下的大雨，\n让我无法再向前迈出一步。%K%P
All I had left now...%K%P
只是，现在…%K%P
Next to a small, shuttered-down grocery store, I spotted\none of the few public phones in the city -- the sole line\nof connection from me to the rest of the world.%K%P
只有位于拉下卷帘门的商店的自动贩售机旁边的、\n数目显著减少的公用电话，\n是我与世界相连的、唯一的线。%K%P
I wanted to hear her voice. I wanted to cry quietly enough\nthat she wouldn't be able to hear.%K%P
想要听到声音。\n想要决不让对方听到地、静静地哭泣。%K%P
Producing a one hundred yen coin from my wallet, I dialed\nthe phone number of the person on my mind.%K
我从钱包里取出了百元硬币，\n拨出了刚才出现在脑海里的电话号码。%K
Terrace House Hinosaka
Terrace House阳之坂
Kaya's mobile phone
夏夜的手机
